closure_audit
  issue 1138
  purpose "The honest count of distinct semantic references in seed data that resolve to no defined meaning, grounded source or override. Declaration identities, comments and literal matcher operands are classified by data/meta/total-closure-schema.lino and are not reference edges; the generator's own output is excluded from the definition set."
  plan "docs/case-studies/issue-1138/plans/09-handler-migration-ratchet.md leaves 6-8"
  defect "The total-closure metric is self-satisfying today. scripts/close-total.py writes data/seed/closure-generated-NN.lino and scripts/audit-total-closure.py then counts those generated glosses as definitions, so the gap it reports is zero by construction while 3,555 English-only glosses no runtime loads stand in for grounding."
  checker "tests/unit/total_closure.rs::seed_closure_gap_only_shrinks"
  measure_source "python3 scripts/audit-total-closure.py --json . reporting unresolved_distinct_honest"
  strict_direction "down. A value above the ceiling fails with grew; a value below it fails with improved, lower the reviewed ceiling. The rule is copied from scripts/check-minimal-core-boundary.rs lines 286-290."
  gate "data/meta/ci-gates/check-closure-audit.lino, running python3 scripts/check-closure-audit.py -- the cheap form of the unit test, so CI can answer the question without building the crate"
  ceiling
    measure unresolved_distinct_honest
    value 1038
    how "distinct unresolved semantic references reported by scripts/audit-total-closure.py. scripts/close-total.py reads the same canonical inventory for its grounding work list. The generated shards are gone as of plan 09 leaf 8, so there is no longer a second number: the honest count and the historical count are the same measurement."
    measured_on 2026-10-07
    note "the first honest run was 3585 over 9135 occurrences, measured with the 16 closure-generated shards still on disk. Plan 09 leaf 8 deleted them, taking the reviewed gap to 3569 over 6342 occurrences after subsequent seed changes. The assembled issue-1138 tree first appeared to grow that gap to 3902, but the increase was entirely a measurement defect: 187 full-line comments were parsed as data, while thousands of local response, pattern, family and evidence-group declaration identities and literal matcher operands had always been treated as meaning references. data/meta/total-closure-schema.lino now declares 32 identity-bearing heads and four literal-operand heads; structural code excludes an identity only on a branch, so a leaf such as intent greeting remains audited. The corrected inventory excludes 2777 distinct declaration identities and 107 distinct literal operands, and scripts/close-total.py reads that same inventory rather than maintaining a second parser. Thirteen genuine method and selection identifiers introduced or exercised by the assembled runtime are grounded with authored five-field metadata in meanings-agent-actions.lino. Twenty-five response intents introduced when hardcoded runtime messages moved into seed data are also defined there rather than hidden by raising the ceiling. That correction produced the previous reviewed gap of 1102 distinct references over 3926 occurrences against 1218 honest defined meanings. On 2026-09-18 the plan 10 routing work grew the honest measure to 1123 -- eight new selection identifiers in the capability-routing table (glob, read_many, multi_edit, todo, subagent, path_set, task_list, delegation) plus callable, which the assembled tree had exercised since the reviewed value was recorded -- and the same rule applied: the growth is grounded, not ceilinged. All thirty-five declared routing-vocabulary identifiers that the audit counted as references (the table's capabilities, objects, acts, loci, and its default ask, plus callable) are now defined with authored five-field metadata in meanings-routing-vocabulary.lino, a seed part the runtime embeds. The reviewed gap stands at 1088 distinct references over 3936 occurrences against 1312 honest defined meanings. This is genuine grounding, not a claim that the excluded schema data became meanings. The 2026-09-21 role-registry regeneration grounded the last four ungrounded role declarations, taking the reviewed gap to 1084. Re-measured 2026-09-30 for the bulk QA, reasoning, and coding batch (issues #1172-#1177, #1181): the new text-transform, statistics, unit, code-task, and quantities seed parts introduced vocabulary faster than grounding kept up, peaking the honest measure at 1093, and the same rule applied in reverse -- thirty-four of the introduced English lemmas were grounded for real against Open English WordNet 2024 through scripts/ground-wordnet.py (wellbeing, secondary, padded, case, trimmed, boolean, integer, float, none, accuracy, adapter, analogy, analyze, append, archive, array, article, ascending, assemble, association, attached, attachment, authentic, authenticate, automatic, average, below, blocked, bound, bounds, brief, bundle, cap, ceiling), taking the reviewed gap to 1059 over 3822 occurrences. Final same-day true-up after the integration landings: the issue #1175 phrase-vocabulary seed and the conventional-commits registry record introduced nineteen more value tokens than that measure carried, while the variance wiktionary entry grounded for real from the recovered API, so the reviewed gap records the measured 1064 over 3837 occurrences; the thirteen common English function words of the phrase vocabulary (about, but, for, me, my, our, these, they, those, via, we, without, your) await their wordnet pass as the one open follow-up. Proper-noun and product identifiers the lexicon has no entry for (javascript, php, wikipedia, github, fizzbuzz, fibonacci, and the eight words dictionaryapi.dev still owes: digits, gallons, median, ounces, pays, spaces, variance, yards) remain honestly unresolved rather than papered over; the same batch also repaired the importer's FAST_BIN and cargo fallback paths, which still pointed at the pre-L1 target/ layout and made every grounding run exit on its first lemma. Re-measured 2026-10-07 for the qa-reasoning-coding bulk-fixes batch: the new SI-dimension, creative-composition, page-formalization, code-node-decomposition, legality, toolchain, small-model, telemetry-consent and multilingual-response seed parts took the honest measure to 1472, and the same rule applied -- the growth was resolved by root cause, not ceilinged. Most of it was a measurement defect in the new data: the 370 surface rows of si-unit-dimensions.lino are recognition strings matched lowercase against the input, so they are now written as quoted literal strings like the quoted cli and gui surface rows of client-integrations.lino (surface itself stays a declaration-identity head, because coding-idioms.lino and the meanings files use it for semantic references), removing 60 distinct tokens. data/meta/total-closure-schema.lino gains five literal-operand heads whose every seed usage is matcher syntax -- command_verb (command-line openers in page-formalization-rules.lino), cst_node_kind (tree-sitter node kind names), output_call and entry_name (per-language code identifiers in code-example-parts.lino), key (TOML/YAML/JSON keys in statement-audit-exclusions.lino; the one other key line is a meaning slug with no value) -- and one declaration-identity head, generated_version, whose first value names a toolchains.lino baseline record with children, removing 46 more. Twenty-three intents are defined with authored five-field metadata in meanings-response-intents.lino: the 21 response intents of the creative-tasks, formalization, legality, repair, product-search and TRIZ response files, and the routing intents product_search and triz_resolution. Finally 294 English lemmas the seed uses in their dictionary sense were grounded for real against Open English WordNet 2024 (the build_record projection of scripts/ground-wordnet.py, the .lino written by a byte-exact replica of json_cache_file verified against all 372 existing wordnet pairs): unit names such as hectare, joule, newton, pascal, watt, hertz, torr and kibibyte, plus vocabulary such as plagiarism, veracity, haiku, sonnet, limerick, church, museum and market for the itinerary planner, shell objects and statistics words. Tokens whose WordNet record names a different sense were deliberately left unresolved rather than grounded -- auxiliaries (am, are, did, has, was, were, will), abbreviations and letters (cd, e, ed, er, g, kt, md, mv, ps, r, rg, y), command and tool names (cat, curl, echo, git, head, kill, pip, tail, tar, touch, yarn, clang), language and product names (lean, lino, swift, gemma, mit, material, bootstrap), Spanish numerals (dos, once), and code literals (true, false, main, assert, max); the underscore unit identifiers (square_meter, kilometer_per_hour, us_gallon and the like) and the four SI base-quantity names remain open too. The reviewed gap records the measured 1049 over 3933 occurrences against 1527 honest defined meanings. Same-day R1017 small-math true-up: the calendar, primality, list-result, glued-operator and synthesis-response seed parts took the honest measure to 1102, and it was resolved by grounding, not ceilinged. Twenty English lemmas used in their dictionary sense were grounded against Open English WordNet 2024 with the same build_record projection and byte-exact codec replica (re-verified against all 666 existing pairs): percentile, prime, hidden, last, older, recursive, superlative, verb, location, containment and the month abbreviations jan, feb, mar, apr, aug, sep, sept, oct, nov, dec. Thirteen response intents (calendar_date_weekday, the numeric_list_result and number_primality families, meta_explanation_why, how_it_works_prior_topic, how_it_works_no_context, network_snapshot, source_refresh) are defined in meanings-response-intents.lino; eleven shell cue roles and classes of code-task-cues.lino (infinite_loop, screen_execution, command_head, prose_lead, size_qualifier, search_object, pattern_lead, suffix_lead, ignore_case, names_only, files_noun) in meanings-code-task-templates.lino; and the meta-reasoner filters and selector keep_greater, keep_less, keep_containing and maximum_by in meanings-agent-actions.lino, all with authored five-field metadata. The schema gains two literal-operand heads whose every seed usage is matcher syntax: ending (inflection suffix rewrites in meta-reasoning.lino, removing est, iest, e, ed, er, ies, ing, ly and y) and members (the vowel character sets of operation-vocabulary.lino, removing aeiou). Left honestly open: percentiles, jun, jul and chars, which OEWN 2024 has no lemma for and dictionaryapi.dev could not serve (HTTP 522), and local_record_store, a sources-registry kind added concurrently. The reviewed gap records the measured 1045. Re-measured 2026-10-07 for the #1177 sed and HAVING breadth: the two new slugs sed and substitute_with are defined with authored five-field metadata in meanings-code-task-templates.lino, and the measure fell to 1044, so the reviewed gap records it. Issue 1175 R3 (classes b, c and e): the new claim rows ground their 38 evidence kinds and 33 handler slugs in five-field records of data/seed/meanings-routing-vocabulary.lino, and five slugs other seeds already named resolve with them, so the gap falls from 1044 to 1039. The issue 1175 R3 follow-up round grounds its 16 new evidence kinds and the handler slugs its rows name for the first time, and fact_lookup with them, so the gap falls to 1038."
